Scenario Behaviour No ETag provided Last-write-wins. The write always succeeds. Matching ETag Write succeeds. State is updated. Mismatched ETag Fails with <code>StatusCode.Aborted</code>. Re-read and retry. <code>create_only: true</code>, empty ETag Succeeds only if the key does not exist; otherwise <code>Aborted</code>. <p>An ETag of <code>"0"</code> is rejected with <code>InvalidArgument</code> — it is the Redis component's force-write sentinel and would silently defeat the compare-and-swap.</p> <pre><code>var current = await client.GetStateAsync("workmanager", "workmanager.worker.abc123");
await client.SaveStateAsync("workmanager", "workmanager.worker.abc123", newValue,
                            etag: current.Etag);
// Throws RpcException with StatusCode.Aborted if the ETag doesn't match.
</code></pre>
